    "title": "What stores are open Easter Sunday 2026? Information on Target, Costco and other retailers",
    "text": "NewsTarget locations nationwide will be closed on Sunday in observance of Easter.(AP Photo/Ted Shaffrey, File)By Jillian Delaney | jdelaney@siadvance.comSTATEN ISLAND, N.Y. — While not recognized as a federal or state holiday, some stores choose to observe Easter, and will shut their doors to patrons on Sunday, April 5. That might not bode well for those who need to pick up that last-minute gallon of milk or chocolate bunny. According to RetailMeNot, grocery stores like Aldi, Costco, Sam’s Club, and Target will close Easter Sunday nationwide. The grocery stores that will be open for the holiday include: BJ’s Wholesale Club, Walmart, Wegmans, and Whole Foods. Have a fashion emergency? Skip J.C. Penney, Marshalls, Macy’s, and TJ Maxx; they all will be shuttered. The Staten Island Mall, New Springville, will be closed.The same goes for décor, entertainment, or electronics — Best Buy, The Container Store, Dick’s Sporting Goods, Home Goods, Hobby Lobby, Lowe’s, and Office Depot won’t be open. Opt for IKEA, Staples, or Home Depot instead. Luckily for pet owners, Petco and PetSmart will be open should your furry or scaly or feathered companion need an extra-special Easter treat. After-dinner coffee can be covered by Starbucks, too; the coffee giant will remain open for all your Easter needs. As for government offices and agencies, don’t expect much. Sunday is a traditional day off for offices like the DMV and Social Security, and they will remain closed on Easter. Garbage, recycling, and organics collection will follow a normal schedule, as well. The Staten Island Advance will publish Easter Sunday for all of your news needs. Jillian Delaney is an award-winning journalist with a master’s degree in Journalism Innovation from Syracuse University. She is a native Staten Islander who reports on local news, data, national politics, and...",
